[phone] After combined install: add module:connections on an owner-chosen home page via canvas placement; verify real configured peers, core Design Canvas, VPN loss versus auth refusal, helper stale/asleep/paused, source freshness and actual notification permission/channel state. Owner enables alerts in context. Controlled test outage only on an idle test service: wait debounce, observe one local Android alert even with tunnel down, dismiss without repeat, restore externally and verify one recovery. Confirm intentional pause stays quiet and closing detail leaves checks running. Do not stop active builds/agents, toggle security/debugging, reboot hosts or install from this lane. Successful automatic restart remains unavailable until a supported guarded host-control API is deployed.
[phone] After install: open Connections on the home page and leave the sheet open for over two minutes: no row says Stale while the monitor's checks are fresh (the journal's last_seen and /services stamps are current), and the flag at the upper right of CONNECTION CHECK opens and closes the check.
[phone] In Connections, Models lists Claude Code, Codex and Grok with a health word from their real runs (no sign-in check, no test call); Codex shows its model where Soma knows it; a missing needed agent says Missing and counts as an incident; the Mac and MG1 runners and phone Linux checks still show under Device connections with Restore.
[phone] In Connections, GitHub shows one reading per device that pushes (Mac Pro, MacBook, MG1, this phone): after a deliberate gh auth logout on one device it names that device with Run gh auth login within 15 minutes, and Restore is not offered; GitHub being down reads as unreachable, not as a login problem. Disk space shows free space for each device; Agent mail shows no stuck mail; Messages says Can't tell unless the iMessage watcher is down; the phone keeper reads Healthy (or a plain 'not running' that Soma fixes by itself).
